    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Like [[p0]], but reads back the existing configuration first and only makes changes that are explicitly different between the configuration file and the interface. This is much less efficient than [[p1]], but has the benefit of not disrupting current peer sessions. The contents of [[p2]] must be in the format described by [[p3]]CONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT[[p4]] below.",
