        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "help"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Shows usage message.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "CONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The configuration file format is based on [[p0]]. There are two top level sections -- [[p1]] and [[p2]]. Multiple [[p3]] sections may be specified, but only one [[p4]] section may be specified.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "INI"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Interface"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Peer"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Peer"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Interface"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] section may contain the following fields:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Interface"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "PrivateKey — a base64 private key generated by [[p0]]wg genkey[[p1]]. Required.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "ListenPort — a 16-bit port for listening. Optional; if not specified, chosen randomly.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "FwMark — a 32-bit fwmark for outgoing packets. If set to 0 or \"off\", this option is disabled. May be specified in hexadecimal by prepending \"0x\". Optional.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] sections may contain the following fields:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "Peer"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0037",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "PublicKey — a base64 public key calculated by [[p0]]wg pubkey[[p1]] from a private key, and usually transmitted out of band to the author of the configuration file. Required.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0038",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "PresharedKey — a base64 preshared key generated by [[p0]]wg genpsk[[p1]]. Optional, and may be omitted. This option adds an additional layer of symmetric-key cryptography to be mixed into the already existing public-key cryptography, for post-quantum resistance.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "AllowedIPs — a comma-separated list of IP (v4 or v6) addresses with CIDR masks from which incoming traffic for this peer is allowed and to which outgoing traffic for this peer is directed. The catch-all [[p0]] may be specified for matching all IPv4 addresses, and [[p1]] may be specified for matching all IPv6 addresses. May be specified multiple times.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "0.0.0.0/0"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "::/0"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Endpoint — an endpoint IP or hostname, followed by a colon, and then a port number. This endpoint will be updated automatically to the most recent source IP address and port of correctly authenticated packets from the peer. Optional.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "PersistentKeepalive — a seconds interval, between 1 and 65535 inclusive, of how often to send an authenticated empty packet to the peer for the purpose of keeping a stateful firewall or NAT mapping valid persistently. For example, if the interface very rarely sends traffic, but it might at anytime receive traffic from a peer, and it is behind NAT, the interface might benefit from having a persistent keepalive interval of 25 seconds. If set to 0 or \"off\", this option is disabled. By default or when unspecified, this option is off. Most users will not need this. Optional.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "CONFIGURATION FILE FORMAT EXAMPLE",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This example may be used as a model for writing configuration files, following an INI-like syntax. Characters after and including a '#' are considered comments and are thus ignored.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] [Interface] [[p1]] PrivateKey = yAnz5TF+lXXJte14tji3zlMNq+hd2rYUIgJBgB3fBmk= [[p2]] ListenPort = 51820",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0045",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] [Peer] [[p1]] PublicKey = xTIBA5rboUvnH4htodjb6e697QjLERt1NAB4mZqp8Dg= [[p2]] Endpoint = 192.95.5.67:1234 [[p3]] AllowedIPs = 10.192.122.3/32, 10.192.124.1/24",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0046",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] [Peer] [[p1]] PublicKey = TrMvSoP4jYQlY6RIzBgbssQqY3vxI2Pi+y71lOWWXX0= [[p2]] Endpoint = [2607:5300:60:6b0::c05f:543]:2468 [[p3]] AllowedIPs = 10.192.122.4/32, 192.168.0.0/16",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0047",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] [Peer] [[p1]] PublicKey = gN65BkIKy1eCE9pP1wdc8ROUtkHLF2PfAqYdyYBz6EA= [[p2]] Endpoint = test.wireguard.com:18981 [[p3]] AllowedIPs = 10.10.10.230/32",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "br"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0048",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DEBUGGING INFORMATION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0049",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sometimes it is useful to have information on the current runtime state of a tunnel. When using the Linux kernel module on a kernel that supports dynamic debugging, debugging information can be written into [[p0]](1) by running as root:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "dmesg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0050",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] # modprobe wireguard && echo module wireguard +p > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control[[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0051",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "On OpenBSD and FreeBSD, debugging information can be written into [[p0]](1) on a per-interface basis by using [[p1]](1):",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "dmesg"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "ifconfig"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0052",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] # ifconfig wg0 debug[[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "strong"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0053",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "On userspace implementations, it is customary to set the [[p0]] environment variable to [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "LOG_LEVEL"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "verbose"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0054",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0055",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "WG_COLOR_MODE"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0056",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If set to [[p0]], always print ANSI colorized output. If set to [[p1]], never print ANSI colorized output. If set to [[p2]], something invalid, or unset, then print ANSI colorized output only when writing to a TTY.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "always"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "never"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "auto"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0057",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "WG_HIDE_KEYS"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0058",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If set to [[p0]], then the pretty-printing [[p1]] sub-command will show private and preshared keys in the output. If set to [[p2]], something invalid, or unset, then private and preshared keys will be printed as \"(hidden)\".",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "never"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "show"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "always"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0059",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "WG_ENDPOINT_RESOLUTION_RETRIES"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0060",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If set to an integer or to [[p0]], DNS resolution for each peer's endpoint will be retried that many times for non-permanent errors, with an increasing delay between retries. If unset, the default is 15 retries.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "em",
            "text": "infinity"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0061",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "SEE ALSO",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0062",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]](8), [[p1]](8), [[p2]](8), [[p3]](8), [[p4]](8).",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "wg-quick"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "ip"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "ip-link"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "ip-address"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "ip-route"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0063",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0064",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]] was written by Jason A. Donenfeld. For updates and more information, a project page is available on the [[p1]].",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "strong",
            "text": "wg"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "World Wide Web",
            "href": "https://www.wireguard.com/"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
